This started out as a typically helpless request for compiling aid,
but I managed to putz about with the sources enough to get things
working and figured I should report what I did to get things working.

For starters, I installed DJGPP & all the needed packages to the same
directory, put the Nethack 3.4.3 source code in a src subdirectory of
that, then followed the install instructions and was mindful of Rob
Ellwood's further instructions, found in a Google search, in:

http://groups.google.com/groups?hl=en&lr=&ie=UTF-8&selm=3CC9D696.8C475E21%40shaw.ca

I also followed the compiling directions I found, but I still had two
problems:

1. Files y.tab.c and y.tab.h, apparently created in the util/
directory during the install process, were not named as expected. 
Apparently another file expects to find them as y_tab.c and y_tab.h. 
Manually renaming them and restarting make seemed to work.  Doing a
search through the source for "y_tab.c" finds no hits, so I'm stumped
as to why this happens.

2. There was a file, dgn_comp.h I think it was (for some reason the
DJGPP tools work weird with the WinXP command prompt window so I can't
scroll back to check), was not found.  I ended up moving this into the
util/ directory and the compile was able to finish.

Any ideas as to what I did wrong in the first place to make these
problems crop up?

